Reclaim disk space: prune orphaned blobs and vacuum the database

Usage: hh gc [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --no-vacuum  Skip the (slow, disk-hungry) VACUUM; only prune orphaned blob files and stale rows. VACUUM rebuilds `hh.db` and needs temporary free space, so use this on a nearly-full disk
      --json       Emit machine-readable JSON instead of plain lines
  -h, --help       Print help

Examples:
  hh gc              prune orphaned blobs, then vacuum
  hh gc --json       machine-readable report
  hh gc --no-vacuum  prune only; skip the slow VACUUM
